frac_filled -1.409764 0.06423454 -21.94713 2.152317e-80
JPF only:              Estimate Std. Error   t value     Pr(>|t|)
(Intercept)  1.364925 0.03528424  38.68369 1.823882e-39
frac_filled -1.449762 0.07098699 -20.42292 3.308142e-26
Non-JPF only:              Estimate Std. Error   t value     Pr(>|t|)
(Intercept)  1.109084 0.05587652  19.84884 8.812426e-68
frac_filled -1.357487 0.07266966 -18.68024 1.001987e-61

JPF median ratio_to_bio12: 3.634461  | Non-JPF median: 0.9971798 
Interpretation: a significant, substantial frac_filled slope shared across the whole
 network would indicate a gap-fill-driven (batch) effect; JPF's elevated median
 holding even among LOW-frac_filled (mostly-measured) sites, with no comparable
 slope explaining it, would indicate a genuine mixture (JPF sites are drawn from a
 wetter/more-error-prone population), not a fill-driven artifact.
